        <body>
            <div xml:id="d107">

                <pb facs="0262" n="230" xml:id="pg230"/>

                <head>107. Memorandum From the Executive Secretary of the National Security Council
                    (Smith) to the President’s Special Assistant (Rostow)<anchor n="1"
                        xml:id="d107-f1"/>
                </head>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName>Washington</placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1967-01-19">January 19, 1967</date>.</dateline></opener>
                <p rendition="#flush">
                    <hi rendition="#italic">For your clearance.</hi>
                </p>
                <p>This cable replies to Win Brown’s reluctance to ask Park now to commit another
                    Korean combat division to Vietnam in 1967.</p>
                <p>It asks Brown’s views on the suggestion that he get Park’s tentative commitment
                    now, before the Korean elections, to deploy another division later this
                    year.</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>
                        <hi rendition="#bold"> BKS </hi>
                    </signed>
                </closer>


                <xi:include href="d107-a1.xml" xpointer="d107-a1"/>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
    <standOff>
        <listAnnotation>
            <note corresp="#d107-f1" n="1" type="source" xml:id="d107-f1-content">
                <p>Source: Johnson Library, National Security File, Country File, Korea, Vol. IV.
                    Top Secret. According to an attached memorandum from Donald Ropa of the NSC
                    Staff to Smith, January 19, both he and Walter Jenkins of the NSC Staff did not
                    object to the proposed telegram.</p>
            </note>
        </listAnnotation>
    </standOff>
